Z||000000||Monkeyman||01-22-2000||04:42 PM||||It's snowing here.  Again!  So far we have about a foot and a half on the ground and it's still coming down hard.  I'm getting a little tired of this.  I have to park my baby in the street and now you can't see it! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  BTW-it's black and should be easy to see in the F*@&!#& snow!  I've shoveled the walk 3 times today and broken 2 ice scraper/snow brushes (now we have a cool aluminum handled one from Autozone!)  It was 7F yesterday and almost 10F today.  Wow!  What a heat wave.  I got a call from the city about 2 hours ago asking if I would kindly move my car off of the street so they wouldn't hit it if they ever decide to plow (only been plowed once so far!--the city mgr lives a couple blocks down the street and it's always plowed right to his front door.  Amazing how the plow must break about the same place everytime, huh!)  After spending 45 min backing my wifes car up the driveway and then trying to get it unstuck, I decided to leave my poor baby right were is was.  Just babbling.  Don't mind me.||||reg||13
