Z||000017||mshill||01-24-2000||04:50 PM||||Deer_slayer,  I saw the sun on Saturday.  And yes, the sky is still blue.  It has really started to rain here on the west coast. It has been raining since late Saturday night and they are talking about flooding in certain areas of Sacramento, CA.<P>I got drenched this afternoon just taking my  2.8 block/heads/flywheel and rotors into the machine shop.  My wife is thrilled that I have a project (86SE engine rebuild) while it is raining cause I get to be a real pain in the *$$ when the sun don't shine.  I am certain that if I lived in the mid-west I would be divorced.<P>I love California!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000018||theogre||01-24-2000||09:37 PM||||I forgot to spray my door seals the other day,,,, got froze out on one side.<P>Spray the locks with WD40. Don't use Liquid Wrench, it freezes. WD-40 pushes out the water and usually won't freeze. ((CRC 5-56 is good but freezes before WD-40 will. Liquid Wrench will freeze above 0F.))<P>Get some of that washer fluid with the antifreeze in it and put in in a spray bottle.. not the usual blue junk. when you park the car spray the glass. If the door seals are wet spray/wipe them with it too.<P>Don't wipe off the glass. The antifreeze will help keep the ice from sticking so hard, or not at all depending on the weather.<P>To break the ice, score it with the scrappers teeth, then let the washer juice soak in.<P>A whole gallon of the washer is about 3$us, even the Rain-X added one is only about that. BTW I found the Rain-X yellow washer fluid actually applies a better coat of Rain-X and it doesn't make my wipers jump all over like regular rain-x does. A little can of the spray deicer, that usually doesn't work as good, is 2$us or more for only about a pint.<P>The only other thing I do is use good tires, and put a 40pound bag of whatever up front to even out the load up front.||||reg||1
